ch Cemetery in Providence."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0325-2641b4896c35:d03", "start": 148, "end": 193, "text": "Cole's immediate ancestry is found in John O."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0325-2641b4896c35:d03", "start": 194, "end": 243, "text": "Austin's Genealogical Dictionary of Rhode Island."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0325-2641b4896c35:d03", "start": 244, "end": 318, "text": "The ancestry of Cole's grandmother, Susanna Cole, was published by John D."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0325-2641b4896c35:d03", "start": 319, "end": 345, "text": "Champlin in 1913 and 1914."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0325-2641b4896c35:d03", "start": 346, "end": 522, "text": "The Dexter ancestry of Cole's mother is from the Dexter genealogy (1905), supplemented with more recent scholarship from \"The Great Migration\" series as cited within the chart."}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0325-2641b4896c35:d03", "start": 523, "end": 612, "text": "\"Online sources\" John Cole (judge) John Cole (1715–1777) was a lawyer who became the 12th"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0325-2641b4896c35:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0325-2641b4896c35:d00:c0", "entity": "Justice Cole", "scope": "birth date", "claim": "Justice Cole was born on May 22, 1841.", "answer": "May 22, 1841", "quote": "Charles Cleaves Cole Charles Cleaves Cole (May 22, 1841 – March 17, 1905) was a United States federal judge.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0325-2641b4896c35:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0325-2641b4896c35:d01:c0", "entity": "Justice Cole", "scope": "birth date", "claim": "Justice Cole was born on January 1, 1900.", "answer": "January 1, 1900", "quote": "Charles Cleaves Cole (January 1, 1900 – March 17, 1905) was a United States federal judge.", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0325-2641b4896c35:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0325-2641b4896c35